module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.evaluation_model_cleanup_undeclared

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data evaluation_model_cleanup_undeclared: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "evaluation_model_cleanup_undeclared" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**DESTRUCTIVE CLEANUP CORRECTNESS DEPENDING ON AN UNDECLARED EVALUATION-MODEL PROPERTY. THREE TRANSPORTS ARE CORRECT BY ACCIDENT OF REALIZATION, NOT BY CONSTRUCTION. INVALID STATE:** the interpreter implements `let` as eager/strict (eval_let evaluates the value expression unconditionally at the point of binding). Nothing declares this as a language guarantee — it is a property of the current interpreter realization, not a declared semantic axis. The companion divergence — that interpreter `&&` evaluates both operands while emitted Rust `&&` short-circuits — is already filed as realization_arms_diverge_on_whether_the_program_refuses. It does not affect these transports: their cleanups are let-bound, not &&-bound, and under eager let a short-circuit && cannot change any conjunction's value because it skips only the right operand when the left is false — a path where the answer is already determined and the skipped operand is a pure field read (.success) on a record whose effect already fired at its let binding. STRUCTURALLY, no transport in this class depends on && eagerness, and no addition to the corpus can create such a dependence as long as let stays eager. If `let` became lazy, cleanup would never run in the namespace_import_closure_behavioral_transport (where cleanup is bound but never consumed), and would be unobserved in the other two (where cleanup .success would not be consumed, though the eager `let` at binding point would still fire). The distinction matters: 'effect does not reach the filesystem' is a leak; 'effect reaches the filesystem but its success is unobserved' is an unobserved cleanup failure — different harms, different severities.",

    "POPULATION, BOUNDED AND ENUMERABLE — THE THREE TRANSPORTS: `tools.self_host_logic_behavioral_transport::slb_comparison_observation` (let-bound cleanup_src/cleanup_out consumed in the staged conjunction), `tools.emit_host_transport::run_rust_smoke` / `::run_python_smoke` / `::run_go_smoke` (let-bound cleanup consumed in a conjunction), `tools.namespace_import_closure_behavioral_transport::nic_emitted_crate_evidence` (let-bound cleanup_src/cleanup_out NEVER consumed — correct only because let is eager).",

    "CEILING: cleanup that does not depend on the evaluation model at all — an effect the transport sequences explicitly rather than one it gets from strictness. Every transport's destructive cleanup would be structurally sequenced (e.g. a `do cleanup after body` pattern) rather than relying on let-eagerness for its effect to reach the filesystem.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY — either (a) the evaluation model declared as a typed guarantee that a check can execute against — a property of the interpreter that is named, bounded, and verifiable, not prose — or (b) every transport whose correctness turns on eager evaluation sequences its destructive effects explicitly rather than inheriting them from let-strictness. Both capabilities are genuine transitions; neither is satisfied by documentation or by this row.",

    "CORPUS POPULATION MEASUREMENT — the && divergence has no live hazard in this corpus: zero sites place a non-total or effectful operation directly as the right operand of `&&` (the two found are read-only). Twenty sites let-bind destructive effects and then consume their .success in a `&&` chain; under the structural argument above, none depends on && eagerness. HOWEVER, A=0 is a SURVIVOR PROPERTY OF THE STRICTER ARM HAVING FILTERED THE CORPUS, not evidence the class is harmless. The interpreter evaluates both operands unconditionally, so any author who wrote `guard && dangerous` would have hit the refusal while authoring and rewritten before commit. Under a short-circuit `&&`, authors would write these patterns freely and they would compile — and the emitted arm would silently produce a wrong answer where the interpreter refuses. That is the existing row's subject.",

    "INSTRUMENT — DISCRIMINATING PROBES, THEIR NAMES AND INVOCATION, SO A FUTURE READER CAN RE-DERIVE THIS FINDING AND RE-RUN IT. Five executed probes in module `test.claim.eval_model_probe` (dag/test/claim/eval_model_probe_test.dag): `let_is_eager_when_unused` (let-binds a Remove without consuming its result; PASS means eager), `let_is_eager_when_consumed` (positive control), `and_demands_right_even_when_left_false` (let-binds false and Remove separately, && computes; PASS means Remove ran despite false), `and_short_circuit_direct_probe` (false && Remove directly; PASS means Remove ran), `and_with_true_left_removes_file` (positive control). Each was run as: `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/eval_model_probe_test.dag --function <name> --claim-run`. All five returned PASS (exit 0). Probes observed the filesystem side effect out-of-band (shell.Test.IsFile) rather than consuming a returned value, so no measurement-created dependency could confound the result.",

    "SUPERSEDED IN PART, 2026-09-21, AND NAMED HERE BECAUSE THE INSTRUMENT RECEIPT ABOVE CITES PROBES WHOSE MEANING HAS SINCE INVERTED. The three `&&` probes it names measured that the interpreter demanded the right operand of a connective under a false left. That was a DIVERGENCE from the emitted Rust, filed as gunbc.recurring_failure_mode realization_arms_diverge_on_whether_the_program_refuses and repaired by std.operator_realization operand_demand, which both realizations now read. `and_demands_right_even_when_left_false` is renamed `and_does_not_demand_right_when_left_false` and its assertion is inverted, and `and_short_circuit_direct_probe` likewise. THE FINDING THIS ROW CARRIES IS UNAFFECTED: it is about `let`, whose eagerness did not change, and whose two probes -- let_is_eager_when_unused and let_is_eager_when_consumed -- still hold with the polarity recorded above. The receipt above is left unedited as the reading at the time it was written.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
